        ("Microeconomics & Price Mechanism", "Income Elasticity", "If the quantity demanded of garri falls when consumer real income increases, garri is classified as:", {"A": "An Inferior Good", "B": "A Normal Good", "C": "A Luxury Good", "D": "A Complementary Good"}, "A", "An inferior good has negative income elasticity of demand (demand drops as consumers become richer).", "What do economists call a staple food that people buy less of as their income rises?"),
